  colour: "Colour script v4 (Thomas, Oct 2026 — characters first): the eye finds the people and their faces first, then the one story object, then the background. Plenty of white and pale space, but never white directly behind a white character: every room is a subtle soft tint behind the characters (sage kitchen, blush living room, beige hall, blue bedroom, lilac-grey landing, grey-aqua office) with quiet tonal furniture one step deeper and near-white floors; background lines are thinner and softer than the characters' outlines; rooms hold only their soft wall, their floor and one anchor piece, plus any piece the frame's own action uses; after the faces, the eye goes straight to the story object, drawn large in clean space. Some face close-ups are pure white with nothing behind them — a visual break where the expression carries the line. Strong colour lives on the story objects (the tangerine jar lid, the turquoise phone) and on a few meaning moments: night navy, the storm violet, one peak colour per chapter. The past is a faded grey memory. No orange or peach backgrounds; red only for danger.",
